# Production-Ready Stripe Integration Tutorial

This is the hardened, industry-standard version. Every production gap from the previous plan has been fixed.

## What Makes This Production-Ready

| Security Concern | How It's Handled |
|---|---|
| **Amount tampering** | Server calculates price from DB — client never sends the amount |
| **Fake payment confirmations** | Stripe webhook verifies payment server-side |
| **Lost orders** | Order created as "pending" BEFORE payment, updated to "paid" by webhook |
| **Double charges** | Idempotency keys prevent duplicate PaymentIntents |
| **Returning users** | Stripe Customer objects let users save cards |
| **Payment traceability** | `stripe_payment_intent_id` saved on every order |

## Architecture

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as 📱 App
    participant Edge as stripe-checkout<br/>(Edge Function)
    participant DB as Supabase DB
    participant Stripe as Stripe API
    participant WH as stripe-webhook<br/>(Edge Function)

    User->>Edge: POST {cartItems, type}
    Edge->>DB: Look up meal prices
    Edge->>DB: Create order (status: pending)
    Edge->>Stripe: paymentIntents.create (with idempotencyKey)
    Stripe-->>Edge: {clientSecret}
    Edge-->>User: {clientSecret, orderId}
    User->>User: presentPaymentSheet()
    User->>Stripe: Card details
    Stripe-->>User: ✅ Success
    User->>User: Show success popup

    Note over Stripe,WH: Async (seconds later)
    Stripe->>WH: payment_intent.succeeded webhook
    WH->>WH: Verify Stripe signature
    WH->>DB: UPDATE order SET payment_status = 'paid'
```

